step_details.raw_response:
Thought: The ranking is unstable and several models are highly correlated; pruning redundant models and then weighting by inverse error may reduce noise and improve performance.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The median is best but we can try a simple inverse‑error weighting on the pruned pool to see if it improves the already strong performance.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse-error weights on the pruned pool to see if it beats the median baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"w2","rationale":"inverse-error weighting on the reduced, less redundant pool"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and several models are correlated; a forward‑selection weight that adapts to complementary errors may beat the current median.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","max_steps":20,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: Test a forward‑selection weighted combination using the 3 best models to see if it beats the indistinguishable median baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w3","rationale":"forward selection of top 3 models"}

Thought: The median is best so far, but a weighted inverse‑error on a smaller, less redundant pool (pool3) might reduce variance and improve performance.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool3","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0}

Thought: The leader (median) is indistinguishable from the runner‑up, so accepting it is the safest choice.  
Action: accept  
Action Input: {"attempt_id":"a2","confidence":"high","justification":"Median strategy already achieves the best validation score and the margin to the next best is statistically indistinguishable; no further improvement is expected."}

